eterans Affairs and De-\npartment of Defense health care systems, and representatives from veteran\nand military service organizations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 2","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Mission. The mission of the Task Force shall be to:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) identify ways to improve benefits and services for Department of\nVeterans Affairs beneficiaries and Department of Defense military\nretirees who are also eligible for benefits from the Department of\nVeterans Affairs through better coordination of the activities of the\ntwo departments;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) review barriers and challenges that impede Department of Veterans\nAffairs and Department of Defense coordination, including budg-\neting processes, timely billing, cost accounting, information tech-\nnology, and reimbursement. Identify opportunities to improve such\nbusiness practices to ensure high quality and cost effective health\ncare; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) identify opportunities for improved resource utilization through\npartnership between the Department of Veterans Affairs and the\nDepartment of Defense to maximize the use of resources and infra-\nstructure, including: buildings, information technology and data\nsharing systems, procurement of supplies, equipment and services,\nand delivery of care.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Department of Veterans Affairs shall, to the extent permitted\nby law, provide administrative support and funding for the Task\nForce.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Members of the Task Force shall serve without any compensation\nfor their work on the Task Force. Members appointed from among\nprivate citizens of the United States, however, while engaged in\nthe work of the Task Force, may be allowed travel expenses, in-\ncluding per diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized by law for\npersons serving intermittently in Government service (5 U.S.C.\n5701–5707), to the extent funds are available.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The co-chairs of the Task Force shall appoint an Executive Director\nto coordinate administration of the Task Force. To the extent per-\nmitted by law, office space, analytical support, and additional staff\nsupport for the Commission shall be provided by executive branch\ndepartments and agencies as directed by the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29447 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4(c)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec4(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) The heads of the executive branch departments and agencies shall,\nto the extent permitted by law, provide the Task Force with infor-\nmation as requested by the co-chairs.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29448 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 4(d)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec4(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) At the call of the co-chairs, the Task Force shall meet as necessary\nto accomplish its mission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29448 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 4(e)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec4(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) The functions of the President under the Federal Advisory Com-\nmittee Act, as amended, except for those in section 6 of that Act,\nthat are applicable to the Task Force, shall be performed by the\nDepartment of Veterans Affairs, in accordance with the guidelines\nthat have been issued by the Administrator of General Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29448 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 4(f)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec4(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. Reports. The Task Force shall report its findings and recommendations\nto the President, through the Secretary of Veterans Affairs and Secretary\nof Defense. The Task Force shall issue an interim report in 9 months from\nthe date of the first meeting of the Task Force. The Task Force shall issue\na final report prior to the end of the second year of operation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29448 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 5","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Termination. The Task Force shall terminate 30 days after submitting\nits final report, but no later than 2 years from the date of this order.\nW","original_source":{"page_or_item":"66 FR 29448 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 6","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13214#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (66 FR 29447)","sha256":"95a0fefce95379cb3f9fe9413e043be8cbc4b5ed0d1dd7059ab5f5ea29cf1426","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2001-05-31/pdf/01-13869.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 14 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:13214"}
